   "source": [
    "# Performance Comparison: SA vs PA vs GA\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook reproduces the performance comparison figure from [arXiv:2510.19544](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.19544), benchmarking three annealing algorithms on a 3D Ising spin glass ($L=10$, $N=1000$):\n",
    "\n",
    "- **SA** (Simulated Annealing): standard local Metropolis updates through a temperature schedule.\n",
    "- **PA** (Population Annealing): adds Boltzmann resampling at each temperature step, biasing the population toward low-energy configurations.\n",
    "- **GA** (Global Annealing): augments PA-style annealing with MADE-based global moves that propose full-configuration updates via a learned autoregressive model.\n",
    "\n",
    "We compare $\\Delta E$ (the running minimum energy per spin) as a function of wall-clock time for three different time budgets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "markdown"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
