   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Fixed Parameters\n",
    "\n",
    "All algorithms share the same coupling instance, temperature range, and number of local MC sweeps per step."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Temperature range\n",
    "Tstart = 1.92\n",
    "Tend = 0.1\n",
    "\n",
    "# Local Metropolis sweeps per temperature step\n",
    "local_moves = 15\n",
    "\n",
    "# GA-specific: global MADE moves and training hyper-parameters\n",
    "global_moves = 5\n",
    "num_epochs_start = 40\n",
    "num_epochs_retrain = 1\n",
    "batch_size = 256\n",
    "\n",
    "# Temperature schedule type (logarithmic in T)\n",
    "schedule = \"logT\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# System size: 3D Ising spin glass on an L×L×L cubic lattice\n",
    "L = 10\n",
    "N = L * L * L"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Simulated Annealing\n",
    "\n",
    "SA performs `local_moves` Metropolis sweeps at each temperature. No resampling or global moves."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
     <img src="notebook_images/SA.png" alt="SA Plot" />
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "15 30 logT -1.68819 -1.65397 15.499\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Population size (number of replicas)\n",
    "pop_size = 100_000\n",
    "\n",
    "# number of temperature steps\n",
    "num_temps = 30  \n",
    "\n",
    "# Disorder instance\n",
    "seed = 310411727  # hard instance\n",
    "E_gs = -1.69300   # ground state energy for the hard instance\n",
    "# seed = 10069     # easy instance (uncomment to switch)\n",
    "#E_gs = -1.74178   # ground state energy for the easy instance\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load coupling matrix\n",
    "J = read_couplings(f'./Data/Alpha/Couplings/couplings_L{L}_R1_seed{seed}.txt', N).to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "temperatures, observ, elapsed_time = simulated_annealing(\n",
    "    L, J, pop_size, local_moves, Tstart, Tend, Observables,\n",
    "    num_temps_determiner=num_temps, schedule=schedule\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "minimum = torch.tensor(observ.get_observable_history(\"min_energy\")).min()\n",
    "print(local_moves, f\"{len(temperatures)}\", schedule, f\"{minimum:.5f}\", f'{observ.get_observable_history(\"mean_energy\")[-1]:.5f}', f\"{elapsed_time:.3f}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Population Annealing\n",
    "\n",
    "PA adds a Boltzmann reweighting + resampling step before the MC sweeps at each temperature, concentrating the population near lower-energy states."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    <img src="notebook_images/PA.png" alt="PA Plot" />
   ]
  },
  {
