   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Global Annealing\n",
    "\n",
    "GA trains a lightweight MADE network on the current population at the start and retrains it at each temperature step. Between local MC sweeps, it proposes full-configuration global moves via the learned model, accepted/rejected by a Metropolis criterion that corrects for the proposal bias."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    <img src="notebook_images/GA.png" alt="GA Plot" />
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "5 15 30 logT -1.69300 -1.69268 13.357 152.949\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Population size (number of replicas)\n",
    "pop_size = 100_000\n",
    "\n",
    "# number of temperature steps\n",
    "num_temps = 30  \n",
    "\n",
    "# Disorder instance\n",
    "seed = 310411727  # hard instance\n",
    "E_gs = -1.69300   # ground state energy for the hard instance\n",
    "# seed = 10069     # easy instance (uncomment to switch)\n",
    "#E_gs = -1.74178   # ground state energy for the easy instance\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load coupling matrix\n",
    "J = read_couplings(f'./Data/Alpha/Couplings/couplings_L{L}_R1_seed{seed}.txt', N).to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "temperatures, observ, elapsed_train_time, elapsed_annealing_time = global_annealing(\n",
    "    L, J, pop_size, global_moves, local_moves, Tstart, Tend, Observables,\n",
    "    schedule=schedule,\n",
    "    num_epochs_start=num_epochs_start,\n",
    "    num_epochs_retrain=num_epochs_retrain,\n",
    "    batch_size=batch_size,\n",
    "    num_temps_determiner=num_temps\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "minimum = torch.tensor(observ.get_observable_history(\"min_energy\")).min()\n",
    "print(global_moves, local_moves, f\"{len(temperatures)}\", schedule, f\"{minimum:.5f}\", f\"{observ.get_observable_history('mean_energy')[-1]:.5f}\", f\"{elapsed_train_time:.3f}\", f\"{elapsed_annealing_time:.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Algorithm Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "We sweep over three time budgets by varying `num_temps` (the number of temperature steps). More steps → longer runtime. The `logT` schedule spaces temperatures logarithmically between `Tstart` and `Tend`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each algorithm is run for each setting and we collect the per-step timestamps and running minimum energy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 55,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Keep the population size fixed\n",
    "pop_size = 100_000\n",
    "\n",
    "# Disorder instance\n",
    "seed = 310411727  # hard instance\n",
    "E_gs = -1.69300   # ground state energy for the hard instance\n",
    "# seed = 10069     # easy instance (uncomment to switch)\n",
    "#E_gs = -1.74178   # ground state energy for the easy instance\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load coupling matrix\n",
    "J = read_couplings(f'./Data/Alpha/Couplings/couplings_L{L}_R1_seed{seed}.txt', N).to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Three num_temps settings that produce roughly 15 s, 50 s, and 150 s runtimes\n",
    "# (exact times depend on hardware; adjust if needed)\n",
    "max_time_list = np.array([30, 60, 180])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Storage: results[algo_name] = list of (elapsed_times, running_min) per num_temps\n",
    "results = {\"SA\": [], \"PA\": [], \"GA\": []}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 56,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "SA  num_temps=  62  |  min_E/N = -1.69202  |  time = 32.7 s\n",
      "SA  num_temps= 122  |  min_E/N = -1.69270  |  time = 65.2 s\n",
      "SA  num_temps= 362  |  min_E/N = -1.69287  |  time = 194.1 s\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# factor of conversion between time and temperature depends on hardware\n",
    "time_per_temp = 30/15  # seconds per temperature step (approximate)\n",
    "num_temps_list = (max_time_list*time_per_temp +2).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simulated annealing (SA)\n",
    "for nt in num_temps_list:\n",
    "    temperatures, observ, elapsed_time = simulated_annealing(\n",
    "        L, J, pop_size, local_moves, Tstart, Tend, Observables,\n",
    "        num_temps_determiner=nt, schedule=schedule\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    rt = observ.get_elapsed_times()\n",
    "    rm = observ.get_running_min_energy()\n",
    "    # keep only the entries recorded after start_time (skip the pre-thermalization entry)\n",
    "    results[\"SA\"].append((rt, rm[1:]))\n",
    "    print(f\"SA  num_temps={nt:>4d}  |  min_E/N = {rm[-1]:.5f}  |  time = {elapsed_time:.1f} s\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 62,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
